+## HTTPS
+
+Set `server.protocol` to `https` and supply paths to an existing TLS certificate and private key. The REST API and UI then listen on `server.https_port`, and gRPC uses TLS on `server.grpc_port`.
+
+```yaml
+server:
+  protocol: https
+  https_port: 443
+  cert_file: /etc/flipt/tls/cert.pem
+  cert_key: /etc/flipt/tls/key.pem
+```
+
+Flipt checks that both files exist before starting. The default `http` protocol continues to use `server.http_port` and does not require certificate files.
+
 ## Databases
 
 Flipt supports both [SQLite](https://www.sqlite.org/index.html) and [Postgres](https://www.postgresql.org/) databases as of `v0.5.0`.
